               <p xml:id="idm153">In the concert programme for the first performance, Hartmann wrote the following explanatory note: "The introduction depicts Correggio's lyrical-melancholic sentiments, interrupted by revelations of the holy ideals of his art, - the Allegro the hopes of his life, soon afterwards darkened by discontent, but soon exhilarated by new inner revelations, - the ending describes the death of Correggio and the future grandeur of his name."</p>
